WEBVTT

00:27:00.591 --> 00:27:04.195
And so I'm not sure like,
sort of, chicken and egg --

00:27:04.219 --> 00:27:06.893
which one was driving which,

00:27:06.917 --> 00:27:10.871
at a certain point the belief
can only push you so far.

00:27:10.895 --> 00:27:13.300
And so maybe that's
what we felt there at the end.

00:27:13.324 --> 00:27:15.542
AG: Yeah, I think that's fair.

00:27:15.566 --> 00:27:17.617
It reminds me a little bit
of some research

00:27:17.641 --> 00:27:19.491
by Sandra Cha and Amy Edmondson,

00:27:19.515 --> 00:27:21.676
who studied values-driven organizations

00:27:21.700 --> 00:27:24.971
and found that the more emphasis
leaders put on values,

00:27:24.995 --> 00:27:27.283
the more risk they end up taking

00:27:27.307 --> 00:27:29.693
of being accused of hypocrisy.